1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,680
6:59 a.m. Your alarm goes off.

2
00:00:03,970 --> 00:00:06,908
You slap the snooze button.
Same as every morning.

3
00:00:08,398 --> 00:00:13,297
But this time... the beeping stops.
And so does everything else.

4
00:00:13,887 --> 00:00:16,264
MOM: Nev! You're gonna be late for—

5
00:00:17,414 --> 00:00:21,072
Your mom is frozen on the stairs.
Mid-word. Mid-step.

6
00:00:22,162 --> 00:00:25,742
The orange juice she was pouring
is hanging in the air. Like glass.

7
00:00:27,032 --> 00:00:30,667
The clock says 6:59. And it stays 6:59.

8
00:00:31,557 --> 00:00:34,437
What if your snooze button didn't
give you nine more minutes of sleep...

9
00:00:34,437 --> 00:00:36,917
but nine minutes of frozen time?

10
00:00:36,917 --> 00:00:39,595
For everyone... except you.

11
00:00:40,885 --> 00:00:43,022
Nine minutes later, everything snaps back.

12
00:00:43,312 --> 00:00:47,464
MOM: School! Wait...
why is the juice all over the floor?

13
00:00:48,214 --> 00:00:49,410
So you run some tests.

14
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:54,794
Rule one: every snooze gives you
exactly nine minutes. Nobody else moves.

15
00:00:55,084 --> 00:00:59,655
Rule two: you can press it again.
And again. The minutes stack.

16
00:00:59,945 --> 00:01:03,787
Rule three: if you touch someone...
they can move too.

17
00:01:04,077 --> 00:01:06,274
You find that one out at the bus stop.

18
00:01:06,564 --> 00:01:13,561
JAKE: Bro. Bro! Why is the bus driver a
statue? Why is that bird just... floating?

19
00:01:13,711 --> 00:01:15,524
Jake's hand is still on your shoulder.

20
00:01:15,814 --> 00:01:20,686
JAKE: Okay. Okay. This is the
best day of my life. Hahaha!

21
00:01:21,636 --> 00:01:23,504
Day one, you go wild.

22
00:01:23,794 --> 00:01:27,744
5 snoozes before a math test.
45 extra minutes to study.

23
00:01:27,744 --> 00:01:30,341
You get an A for the first
time since fourth grade.

24
00:01:30,631 --> 00:01:36,484
MR. HALL: Nev... an A? Did you... study?

25
00:01:36,634 --> 00:01:41,521
10 snoozes at lunch. Jake eats
everyone's fries. Every single tray.

26
00:01:41,811 --> 00:01:46,314
JAKE: It's not stealing if time is frozen.
The law is frozen, bro. Hahaha!

27
00:01:46,464 --> 00:01:48,626
You make him put them back. Mostly.

28
00:01:48,916 --> 00:01:53,350
20 snoozes at night. 3 hours of video
games while the whole world waits.

29
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:58,435
By Friday, you've stacked
140 snoozes. 21 extra hours.

30
00:01:58,725 --> 00:02:01,795
Your week has eight days in it.
And nobody notices.

31
00:02:02,885 --> 00:02:08,964
Saturday, you try the big one. 100
snoozes in a row. 15 hours of frozen time.

32
00:02:09,254 --> 00:02:12,359
You walk downtown.
A pigeon is frozen mid-flap.

33
00:02:12,359 --> 00:02:15,964
A guy is frozen mid-sneeze.
You put your hat on him.

34
00:02:16,854 --> 00:02:21,157
A hot dog guy is frozen mid-squeeze.
The ketchup just hangs there in the air.

35
00:02:22,047 --> 00:02:25,300
You eat the hot dog. You leave $5.
You're not a monster.

36
00:02:26,390 --> 00:02:28,232
Day 10, you stop counting.

37
00:02:28,522 --> 00:02:30,147
You sleep in frozen time.

38
00:02:30,147 --> 00:02:33,427
12 hours of perfect sleep,
and you're still early to school.

39
00:02:33,717 --> 00:02:38,659
You read every book in the library. You
learn guitar. You learn Spanish. Kind of.

40
00:02:38,949 --> 00:02:45,349
NEV: Hola. Me llamo Nev. Son las... 6:59.

41
00:02:45,499 --> 00:02:47,056
Jake wants to use it for everything.

42
00:02:47,346 --> 00:02:49,621
JAKE: Dude, freeze the game!
Right before the buzzer!

43
00:02:49,621 --> 00:02:51,538
We walk the ball into the hoop!

44
00:02:52,488 --> 00:02:55,241
You do. The whole gym goes crazy.

45
00:02:56,531 --> 00:03:00,202
Extra time: 900 hours. And counting.

46
00:03:01,692 --> 00:03:05,631
Then, on day 19,
your mom stops you at the door.

47
00:03:05,921 --> 00:03:10,420
MOM: Honey... did you get taller?
Like... since Monday?

48
00:03:10,570 --> 00:03:14,970
You laugh. But at school,
your jeans are too short.

49
00:03:15,260 --> 00:03:19,388
Your hair is longer than Jake's.
You got a haircut two weeks ago.

50
00:03:19,678 --> 00:03:23,875
In the kitchen, there's a door where your
mom marks your height every birthday.

51
00:03:24,765 --> 00:03:29,653
Last mark: September.
Today you're 2 inches above it.

52
00:03:29,943 --> 00:03:34,337
JAKE: Bro... is that a mustache?
Since when do you have a mustache?

53
00:03:35,287 --> 00:03:37,175
That night, you do the math.

54
00:03:37,465 --> 00:03:42,682
900 hours of frozen time. That's 37 days.

55
00:03:42,972 --> 00:03:45,632
37 days that only you lived through.

56
00:03:45,922 --> 00:03:50,865
The calendar says three weeks have
passed. Your body says two months.

57
00:03:51,755 --> 00:03:55,888
Every snooze doesn't just freeze
the world. It moves you forward.

58
00:03:57,178 --> 00:04:01,342
You're getting older...
while everyone you love is standing still.

59
00:04:01,632 --> 00:04:03,164
And it's not just the haircut.

60
00:04:03,454 --> 00:04:05,394
Jake tells you a joke at lunch.

61
00:04:05,394 --> 00:04:08,579
You heard it 40 frozen hours ago.

62
00:04:08,579 --> 00:04:10,259
You forget to laugh.

63
00:04:10,549 --> 00:04:13,284
JAKE: Okay... you used to love that one.

64
00:04:13,434 --> 00:04:15,269
Your mom's birthday is Saturday.

65
00:04:15,269 --> 00:04:20,749
For her, it's two days away.
For you, it's two lonely weeks.

66
00:04:21,839 --> 00:04:24,248
And then you notice something worse.

67
00:04:24,538 --> 00:04:31,053
In frozen time, it's quiet.
No birds. No cars. No voices.

68
00:04:32,543 --> 00:04:35,819
Just you... and a clock that never moves.

69
00:04:36,909 --> 00:04:40,352
You've spent more time alone this
month than with anyone you know.

70
00:04:41,242 --> 00:04:44,416
NEV: Mom? Mom... can you hear me?

71
00:04:45,366 --> 00:04:49,466
She can't. She's frozen in the kitchen,
smiling at something you said...

72
00:04:49,466 --> 00:04:51,105
30 hours ago.

73
00:04:52,395 --> 00:04:54,080
So you try to stop.

74
00:04:54,370 --> 00:04:58,209
Monday morning. 6:59. The alarm rings.

75
00:04:58,499 --> 00:05:02,689
Your hand moves to the snooze
button by itself. Like a habit.

76
00:05:03,779 --> 00:05:08,139
One more. Just nine minutes.
What's nine minutes?

77
00:05:09,229 --> 00:05:11,139
You've pressed it 4,000 times.

78
00:05:12,029 --> 00:05:14,665
You pull the plug. The clock goes dark.

79
00:05:15,855 --> 00:05:18,698
And for the first time in
two months... you're late.

80
00:05:18,988 --> 00:05:21,510
MR. HALL: Nev. You're late.
That's detention.

81
00:05:22,460 --> 00:05:26,818
It's the best detention of your life.
Because the clock on the wall is moving.

82
00:05:27,708 --> 00:05:32,747
Slowly. Normally.
For everyone. Including you.

83
00:05:34,237 --> 00:05:35,783
You tell Jake everything.

84
00:05:36,073 --> 00:05:39,343
JAKE: Wait. So you're two
months older than me now?

85
00:05:39,343 --> 00:05:43,248
So I'm the baby? Hahaha... no way.

86
00:05:43,398 --> 00:05:46,196
You laugh. At the right time.

87
00:05:46,486 --> 00:05:50,016
JAKE: But promise me one thing.
If you ever freeze time again...

88
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:51,458
you take me with you.

89
00:05:51,608 --> 00:05:52,645
You promise.

90
00:05:52,935 --> 00:05:55,600
Saturday, you give your
mom a birthday card.

91
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:59,727
You wrote it on day 12... of frozen time.

92
00:06:00,017 --> 00:06:06,322
MOM: Oh, sweetie... it's beautiful. When
did you find the time to write all this?

93
00:06:07,072 --> 00:06:10,184
You smile. Some secrets are worth keeping.

94
00:06:11,474 --> 00:06:17,305
Extra time: zero. And for the first time,
that number feels good.

95
00:06:18,595 --> 00:06:20,958
That night, you sleep with no alarm.

96
00:06:22,048 --> 00:06:23,968
Until 3:33 a.m.

97
00:06:24,658 --> 00:06:27,685
Beep. Beep. Beep.

98
00:06:28,775 --> 00:06:31,293
The clock you unplugged... is ringing.

99
00:06:32,183 --> 00:06:35,867
On the screen, one word. Snoozed.

100
00:06:36,757 --> 00:06:37,788
You didn't press it.

101
00:06:38,878 --> 00:06:42,830
Outside, the rain is frozen in the air.
The whole street is still.

102
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:49,467
Except for one window across the street...
where somebody just turned on a light.

103
00:06:50,757 --> 00:06:54,254
What would you do with nine frozen
minutes? Tell us in the comments.
